WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.930 --> 00:00:05.939
After Disney fired James Gunn as the director
of Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3 in July

00:00:05.939 --> 00:00:10.930
2018, the threequel film meant to close out
the franchise got pushed onto rocky ground

00:00:10.930 --> 00:00:13.000
and placed on a temporary production halt.

00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:18.160
Now, reports have surfaced that suggest Guardians
Vol. 3 might get completely booted out of

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:22.740
its spot on Marvel's release schedule, with
what's being described as a "surprise MCU

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:23.720
film" replacing it.

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:27.540
So, what is this unforeseen Marvel Cinematic
Universe installment?

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:32.040
According to the folks at ScreenGeek, the
answer is...kind of strange.

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:35.940
"Stop."

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:40.840
ScreenGeek recently picked up on an exclusive
report that The Daily Mirror published in

00:00:40.870 --> 00:00:46.200
mid-August, one that claimed Benedict Cumberbatch
is poised to earn just under $10 million to

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:50.160
top-line a sequel to his 2016 solo superhero
movie Doctor Strange.

00:00:50.380 --> 00:00:54.890
The Daily Mirror further alleged that Marvel
will get Doctor Strange 2 behind cameras in

00:00:54.890 --> 00:00:58.920
spring 2019, estimating that filming "could
take as long as six months."

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:03.290
Taking this nugget of information, ScreenGeek
explored what it could mean for the MCU as

00:01:03.290 --> 00:01:07.900
a whole, coming up with the idea that Doctor
Strange 2 could take precedence over Guardians

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:10.600
of the Galaxy Vol. 3 on Marvel's to-do list.

00:01:10.700 --> 00:01:15.920
The outlet pointed to Cumberbatch's reported
$6.6 million salary increase as a primary

00:01:15.930 --> 00:01:20.310
piece of evidence supporting that idea, and
looked to a mysterious message Doctor Strange

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:24.180
director Scott Derrickson posted to Instagram
as additional corroboration.

00:01:24.420 --> 00:01:28.950
In July, shortly after Gunn's firing, Derrickson
shared an image of Doctor Strange from the

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:30.780
Marvel comic books with the caption:

00:01:30.980 --> 00:01:33.120
"'Not my will, but thine be done…'

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:34.380
See you in September."

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:39.160
Many fans took this to mean that Marvel had
gotten to work on Doctor Strange 2, and that

00:01:39.160 --> 00:01:43.440
the studio would be making a major announcement
regarding the sequel pic sometime in September.

00:01:43.720 --> 00:01:48.060
It would be easy to shut down the idea that
Doctor Strange 2 is really in the works considering

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:51.940
Disney and Marvel haven't made an official
announcement about it or given it a release

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:52.440
date.

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:57.500
However, Marvel Studios president Kevin Feige
did actually reveal that a Doctor Strange

00:01:57.500 --> 00:01:58.540
sequel is happening.

00:01:58.940 --> 00:02:00.760
He told CinemaBlend earlier this year:

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:05.440
"[Doctor] Strange, you know, whenever we do
another Strange one, which we will do, it

00:02:05.450 --> 00:02:09.759
will be a number of years from the first Strange,
and yet he's a very big part of [Avengers:]

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:10.440
Infinity War.

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:14.700
So it is just a good problem to have when
you have too many beloved characters that

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:16.000
people want to see more of."

00:02:16.340 --> 00:02:21.480
Popular speculation is that Marvel will release
Doctor Strange 2 sometime in 2020 - the same

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:25.980
year Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3 was meant
to debut, at least according to Gunn.

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:30.709
If The Daily Mirror's report is to be believed,
a 2020 premiere for Doctor Strange 2 would

00:02:30.709 --> 00:02:31.640
certainly make sense.

00:02:31.940 --> 00:02:37.439
An early 2019 filming start date and a mid-2019
end date would give the filmmaking team at

00:02:37.439 --> 00:02:41.739
least a year to piece together the movie,
add in what's bound to be a ton of CGI, and

00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:42.820
smooth out any kinks.

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:53.500
The real question here, though, is whether
Doctor Strange 2 will actually replace Guardians

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:56.160
of the Galaxy Vol. 3 on Marvel's movie docket.

00:02:56.280 --> 00:03:01.319
Marvel never formally dated Guardians Vol.
3, but the studio does have three dates in

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:06.920
2020 reserved for MCU entries: May 1st, July
31st, and November 6th.

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:11.799
The third Guardians movie could have occupied
any one of those spots, and if Marvel really

00:03:11.799 --> 00:03:16.819
does plan to launch Doctor Strange that year,
the Sorcerer's sequel may have knocked Guardians

00:03:16.820 --> 00:03:18.340
3 out of one of those dates.

00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:22.879
Unfortunately, it's all a big bundle of conjecture
for now, but with Derrickson teasing what

00:03:22.879 --> 00:03:26.549
could be a huge announcement in September,
it appears that things are really heating

00:03:26.549 --> 00:03:28.020
up for the Doctor Strange sequel.

00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:32.510
For the time being, however, Marvel fans can
still look forward to catching Captain Marvel,

00:03:32.510 --> 00:03:35.869
Avengers 4 and Spider-Man: Far From Home in
2019.

